  message: "TIMING DATA from WI-zohuk (2026-10-01, dev 8cfcab7b07, `survey --budgets none --no-handler-slices`, one survey per board slot, box shared with other jobs):\n  nextjs (325 MB): arm B ran 3 h 05 min at ~97% CPU, 4.8 GB RSS, and wrote no survey; stopped by pid under the run's wall-clock rule. So \"does not finish\" now holds at 3 h, not only at 26 min.\n  vscode (186 MB): 7,771 s and 9,056 s (two arms differing by one emptied dict in js_ts.py), 1.22 M edges, a 1.5 GB survey JSON. /proc/<pid>/io showed rchar = 92.9 GB at ~1 h 20 min into the vscode survey with ~8 fds open on vscode/extensions/vscode-colorize-tests/test/colorize-results/*.json and colorize-tree-sitter-results/*.json, rotating over time: ~500x the repository's size read back, which points at a phase re-reading files rather than at parse cost. Not profiled (py-spy needs privileges this box does not grant).\n  For contrast, same flags: lila (185 MB, Scala + TS) 235 s; argo-cd (106 MB) ~200 s; nestjs (17 MB) 40 s. The analyzer-only pass (analyze_javascript) was 670 s on vscode and 821 s on nextjs, so the JS/TS analyzer is a minority of either survey's wall clock."  # 8eb4
